ately* (demonstrating stress resilience), *concentrates very well* (attention and information accuracy), *solves problems extremely well* (technical and cognitive competence and decision quality), and *takes responsibility seriously* (role maturity and responsibility).\nMy concerns about the other candidates are:\n* **Candidate\u202fA** \u2013 while he\u202f*anticipates dangerous situations*, *sees complex connections*, has *excellent spatial vision* and *very good leadership qualities*, the notes also indicate he\u202f*is sometimes not good at taking criticism* (feedback orientation) and can be *unorganized* (operational reliability).\n* **Candidate\u202fB** \u2013 he is described as *very conscientious*, *handles stress very well*, *assesses weather conditions* well and has *excellent computer skills* (technical competence), but the same notes say he can be *grumpy* and *uncooperative* (crew cooperation and professional communication).\n* **Candidate\u202fC** \u2013 he *makes correct decisions quickly*, is *100\u202f% reliable* and *creates a positive atmosphere with his crew* (crew cooperation), yet the notes state he *has difficulty communicating ideas*, is *regarded as egocentric* and is *not very willing to further his education* (communication, adaptability and feedback orientation)."}
