{"id": 35, "ts": 1780447528.3436406, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s overview of Candidate\u202fD and note that while D shows strong technical competence, concentration, and responsibility, both Sarah and Emily flag potential crew\u2011cooperation issues\u2014arrogance, a hot temper, and a \u201cloner\u201d perception. Those concerns are serious for a long\u2011distance cockpit where collaboration is critical.\nGiven that, I\u2019m less convinced D is the safest overall choice. Candidate\u202fC, on the other hand, demonstrates quick, correct decision\u2011making, stays calm in crises, and understands complicated technology\u2014key for stress resilience and technical competence. Although C is described as egocentric and not eager for further education, there is no evidence of disruptive behavior toward crew, and his calmness under pressure directly addresses a core safety criterion.\nTherefore, I shift my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fC**, pending any additional input on his crew\u2011cooperation and adaptability."}
